> values of all discrete population units).
>
> To represent a single population realization, the primary interest is
> not in the posterior distribution of the fixed and hyperparameters,
> but in applying one value for each parameter - an obvious choice would
> be the posterior mean - and having variation generated only through
> the (multivariate) distribution of random effects and residuals as
> implied by the posterior mean hyperparameter values. So values need to
> be drawn from this multivariate distribution, for application to new
> levels of the random effects and for generating new residuals.
